# Hazelcast maintainers report that their shipped JSON paths do not use polymorphic
# typing with a configured type validator, required by CVE-2026-54512 and CVE-2026-54513.
# See https://github.com/hazelcast/hazelcast/issues/26597
# Reviewed Hazelcast 5.7.0 sources and packaged callers: no use of its shaded databind.
# OneDev's own ObjectMapper uses patched Jackson 2.22.2.
CVE-2026-54512
CVE-2026-54513

# Hazelcast 5.7.0 shades jackson-core 2.21.2 and 3.1.2; fixed in 2.21.4 and 3.1.4.
# Reviewed JSON paths use synchronous createParser calls (including jackson-jr);
# no callers of the affected non-blocking parsers were found in the packaged build.
# Reassess these exceptions when changing Hazelcast or its JSON usage.
